onditional use approval expires 6\n                                 December 2026 unless a building permit\n                                 issues, and that date is not recorded in\n                                 either instrument.\n\n\n                         Confidential — prepared for the Township's internal use · Page 4 of 38\n\f                              Conestoga Township | Brightfield Solar Project (CU-2024-006) | Compliance Tracking Matrix\n\n\n4. How to read the status entries\nStatus in Part 1 records only what the six reviewed documents establish as at 15 January 2025. It is\nnot a statement about what has happened in fact.\nStatus                 Meaning                                                                               Shade\nSatisfied (record)     The documents in the file establish compliance on their face. No independent\n                       verification was possible.\nOpen (no evidence)     The condition is due, or will be due, and no evidence of performance appears\n                       anywhere in the file.\nOpen (time-critical)   An open item with a deadline already fixed, in most cases already close.\nOpen (pre-permit       An open item that must be satisfied before a building or grading permit can\ngate)                  lawfully issue.\nVerify (site plan)     Compliance must be read off the approved site plan or a survey, neither of which is\n                       in the file.\nConflict               Two or more reviewed documents state different things, or the condition departs\n                       from the Ordinance. See Part 2.\nGap                    The Ordinance imposes the requirement and the Decision does not carry it forward.\n                       See Part 4.\nN/A                    Not triggered on the designed project, but retained for completeness.\n\nSeverity and rating scales are set out in Appendix C. Two conventions apply throughout: quotations are\nreproduced from the source documents without correction (including their errors), and every figure has been\nrecomputed independently rather than taken from a summary.\n\n\n\n\n                       Confidential — prepared for the Township's internal use · Page 5 of 38\n\f"}
