{"turn": 45, "role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "call_00_k5ktFxNCT4iNqcNuhytY9188", "tool_name": "bash", "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cd $WORKSPACE_DIR && pdftotext -f 34 -l 38 -layout render/compliance-tracking-matrix.pdf - | head -120\"}", "result": "PART 7 — ACTION PLAN\nEighteen actions, sequenced by urgency. Actions P-01 to P-08 can be taken now and do not depend on the applicant. Actions P-09 onwards are\npermit-stage gates. The whole plan is calendar-driven: the two fixed dates are 6 March 2025 (final stormwater plan) and 6 December 2026\n(conditional use expiry), and everything else has to fit between them.\nID      Action                                                                                   Owner                        When                       Priority   Linked refs\nP-01    Issue a document request to the applicant for the site plan, noise and glare studies,    Zoning Officer               Within 7 days              Critical   D-02 - D-09\n        property value report, cultural resources and PNDI correspondence (D-02 to D-09).\nP-02    Obtain a certified copy of the codified Ordinance and re-run Part 3 of this matrix       Solicitor / Zoning Officer   Within 14 days             Critical   I-34, D-01, D-12\n        against it, including the full text of s.(B)(15).\nP-03    Determine the treatment of panel area for the 75% lot coverage ceiling, in writing. If   Township Engineer            Within 14 days             Critical   I-01, RC-10, R-01\n        panels count, begin the amendment/redesign conversation immediately.\nP-04    Reconcile the docket number (CU-2024-006 vs CU-2024-012) with the county and             Zoning Officer               Within 14 days              High      I-21, R-19\n        correct the record.\nP-05    Reconcile the two parcel schedules against the recorded deeds; confirm the lease         Zoning Officer / title       Within 21 days              High      I-04, I-05\n        terms for Parcels -003 and -004.                                                         company\nP-06    Confirm the stormwater submission date to the Conservation District. If 6 March          Township Engineer            Within 7 days              Critical   B-05, B-06, R-05\n        2025 is not achievable, seek a documented Board extension before the date passes.\nP-07    Take a Board decision on the PILOT escalator: amend Condition 30 or accept Year          Solicitor / Board            At next Board meeting      Critical   I-16, RC-15, R-03\n        16. Do not resolve it by side letter.\nP-08    Take a Board decision on the MFN clause and give the Solicitor a documented              Board                        At next Board meeting       High      R-04\n        negotiating mandate, including the fallback positions.\nP-09    Check the site plan dimension for the 500 ft substation/inverter/reference dwelling      Township Engineer            Within 14 days             Critical   I-06, I-11, G-03, R-10\n        setback and the 300 ft BESS property-line setback.\nP-10    Require a wetland delineation and floodplain analysis before the final stormwater        Township Engineer            Before 6 March 2025        Critical   G-09, R-09\n        plan is accepted.\nP-11    Recalculate the agricultural mitigation on NRCS/CD-confirmed acreage and correct         Zoning Officer / Solicitor   Before building permit      High      I-02, RC-04, RC-05, R-02\n        Condition 28 by amendment.\nP-12    Sequence the pre-permit gates (PHMC, USFWS/PFBC, glare, stormwater, PILOT,               Solicitor / Township         Within 30 days             Critical   G-23, RC-13, R-06\n        decommissioning security, parent guaranty, recorded leases, agricultural payment)        Engineer\n        into a dated critical path to 6 December 2026.\nP-13    Consolidate the condition defects identified in Part 3 into a single corrective          Solicitor                    Within 60 days              High      Part 3\n        amendment (G-01 to G-29; I-01 to I-35), so that the Ordinance standards that were\n        omitted or relaxed are restored in one instrument.\nP-14    Require the glaring analysis early, with a mitigation plan subject to Board approval     Township Engineer            Before panel procurement    High      I-13, B-14, R-16\n        where impacts are identified.\nP-15    Obtain written fire company comment on access, turning radii and BESS fire-water         Zoning Officer / Fire        Before permit issuance      High      G-07, G-29, R-11\n        supply, and confirm the gate and lock-box protocol.                                      Company\nP-16    Correct the record-level errors: Finding 7 (standards that do not exist), Finding 20     Solicitor                    Within 30 days             Medium     I-20, I-22, I-25, I-26, I-32,\n        (study author), Finding 16 (job range), the appeal-date recital and the s.609/s.609.1                                                                       I-33\n        citation.\nP-17    Establish the annual compliance calendar: 31 March reporting, annual inspection, 5-      Zoning Officer               Before COD                 Medium     E-02 - E-07, G-19\n        yearly cost estimate update, annual emergency exercise.\nP-18    Record the 6 December 2026 expiry in the permit tracking system with an alert at 12      Zoning Officer               Immediately                 High      G-23, R-06\n        months out.\n\n\nCritical path to the 6 December 2026 permit expiry\nSequence the pre-permit gates in this order. Each is a prerequisite to the next permit, and several run in parallel.\n\f                                                                                            Conestoga Township | Brightfield Solar Project (CU-2024-006) | Compliance Tracking Matrix\nWindow           Gate\nNow              Obtain the certified ordinance and the sealed site plan; re-run the gap analysis against the codified text (P-02, D-01, D-02).\nNow              Confirm the Conservation District stormwater submission date. If 6 March 2025 is unreachable, seek a documented Board extension before the date passes (P-06).\nNow              Commission the wetland delineation and floodplain analysis on the shared survey base (P-10).\nQ1 2025          Resolve the lot-coverage determination and the substation setback dimension. Both may require a layout change, and layout changes take longest (P-03, P-09).\nQ1–Q2 2025       Corrective amendment consolidating the Part 4 gaps and the Part 2 conflicts, including the PILOT escalator if the Board chooses to amend rather than accept Year 16 (P-07,\n                 P-13).\n2025             PHMC determination and USFWS/PFBC bog turtle consultation, working to the seasonal survey windows (B-03, B-04).\nBefore permits   Glare analysis with mitigation plan; parent guaranty; recorded lease memoranda; decommissioning security instrument with rating evidence; executed and recorded PILOT;\n                 agricultural mitigation payment on confirmed acreage; road maintenance agreement and bond (B-14, A-02, A-03, D-02, D-06, B-10, A-24).\nMarch 2026       Building permit issued — comfortably ahead of the 6 December 2026 expiry and consistent with the stated 1 April 2026 construction start.\n\n\n\n\n                                                  Confidential — prepared for the Township's internal use · Page 35 of 38\n\fAPPENDIX A — CONDITION-BY-CONDITION STATUS INDEX\nThe Decision imposes thirty-five numbered conditions. This index maps each condition to the tracked obligation rows in Part 1 and gives its\naggregate status. A condition is 'mixed' where some of its limbs are satisfied on the record and others are open or conflicting.\nCondition        Subject                                                              Tracked in Part 1                          Aggregate status\nCond 1           General compliance with the Site Plan                                A-01      